---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { PRELAUNCH } from '../config';
---
<Base title="Terms of use · Sawaza" description="The Sawaza terms of use: what Sawaza is, what it is not, and what you agree to." bodyId="page-terms">
<style is:global>
#page-terms .prose{max-width:min(100%,64em);columns:1}
#page-terms .prose ul,#page-terms .prose p{max-width:56em}
#page-terms .prose .sum{max-width:56em;margin:28px 0 8px;padding:22px 24px;border-radius:16px;background:var(--panel);border:1px solid var(--line)}
#page-terms .prose .sum h2{margin-top:0;font-size:clamp(20px,2.4vw,26px)}
#page-terms .prose .next-row .tlink{min-height:44px}
#page-terms .draft{display:flex;gap:14px;align-items:flex-start;padding:18px 20px;border-radius:14px;border:1.5px dashed rgba(227,168,43,.6);background:var(--goldsoft);color:var(--ink);font-size:16px;line-height:1.55;margin-bottom:28px}
#page-terms .draft .placeholder{flex:none;margin-top:3px}
#page-terms .prose .pending{color:var(--quiet);font-size:15px}
#page-terms .prose .pending .placeholder{margin-right:6px}
#page-terms .prose h2:first-of-type{margin-top:28px}
</style>
<section class="page-hero" id="top">
  <svg class="watermark" viewBox="0 0 1000 1000" aria-hidden="true"><g fill="currentColor"><path d="M113.394,690.625 L237.500,690.625 A184.375,190.625 0 0 0 421.875,500.000 A340.625,334.375 0 0 1 762.500,165.625 L810.606,165.625 A25.000,25.000 0 0 0 826.950,121.712 A500.000,500.000 0 0 0 12.163,609.619 A103.750,103.750 0 0 0 113.394,690.625 Z"/><path d="M886.606,309.375 L762.500,309.375 A184.375,190.625 0 0 0 578.125,500.000 A340.625,334.375 0 0 1 237.500,834.375 L189.394,834.375 A25.000,25.000 0 0 0 173.050,878.288 A500.000,500.000 0 0 0 987.837,390.381 A103.750,103.750 0 0 0 886.606,309.375 Z"/></g></svg>
  <div class="wrap">
    <div>
      <p class="q">Terms of use</p>
      <h1>The terms, in <em>plain</em> words first.</h1>
      <p class="sub" data-new="1">How Sawaza works, what it does not do, and what we each agree to.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="sec"><div class="wrap"><div class="prose">
  <p class="meta">Last updated 28 October 2026</p>
  <div class="sum"><h2>In short</h2><ul data-new="1"><li>Sawaza keeps one record of money between people, signed by both sides. It never holds or moves money.</li><li>You are responsible for what you write, so write what really happened.</li><li>A signed record is sealed, so any change shows. A correction is a new record that both sides sign.</li><li>When the two sides disagree, both versions are kept. Sawaza is a witness, not a judge.</li><li>Sawaza is free to use and in beta, so it may sometimes be unavailable.</li></ul><p class="meta">The full terms follow. If they differ from this summary, the full terms apply.</p></div><h2>1. These terms</h2><p data-new="1">These terms are an agreement between you and SAWAZA TECHNOLOGIES - SMC LIMITED, a company registered in Uganda under registration number 80047057968423 ("Sawaza", "we", "us"). They apply when you use the Sawaza app or this website. By creating an account, you agree to them. Our <a href="/privacy">privacy policy</a> explains how we handle your data.</p><h2>2. What Sawaza is</h2><p data-new="1">Sawaza keeps one record of money between people, signed by both sides. You write what happened, the other side answers, and when everyone the record names has signed, it is sealed.</p><p data-new="1">Sawaza records money. It never holds it or moves it. It is not a bank, a payment service, a lender or a mobile money provider, and it does not take deposits. Any loan, debt or payment you record is between you and the other party, and Sawaza is not a party to it.</p><h2>3. Your account</h2><ul data-new="1"><li>You must be 18 or over and able to enter into an agreement.</li><li>You sign in with a phone number that is yours. Keep your phone and its lock safe: anyone holding your unlocked phone can act as you in the app.</li><li>If you lose your phone, sign in with the same number on a new phone and your records come back. If you lose the number itself, tell us at hello@sawaza.app.</li><li>One person, one account. Do not sign up with someone else's number or pretend to be someone else.</li></ul><h2>4. The records you write</h2><p data-new="1">You are responsible for what you write. Write what really happened, with the right amount, date and party. Do not use Sawaza to record a debt or payment you know to be false, to pressure someone into signing, or to send records to people who do not deal with you.</p><p data-new="1">A record you send can be confirmed, marked as wrong, or declined by the other side. Until they answer it reads Awaiting. A record only you have signed is your own note, and it does not show that the other side agreed.</p><h2>5. Signed records and disagreements</h2><p data-new="1">A signed record is sealed, so any change shows. A correction is a new record that both sides sign.</p><p data-new="1">When the two sides disagree, the record reads Contested and both versions are kept. Sawaza is a witness, not a judge: we do not decide who is right, collect debts or enforce payments. A sealed record shows that both sides signed the same words, and you may use it as evidence of that. Whether it settles a dispute is for the two of you, or a court, to decide.</p><h2>6. Groups and businesses</h2><p data-new="1">A group or business account acts through the people it names. Admins and officers write and sign for the account and are responsible for doing so honestly on its behalf. Each member confirms their own lines. A household, savings group, cash round or business that uses Sawaza keeps its own rules and agreements: Sawaza keeps the money side of the record, not the meeting, and does not run the group.</p><h2>7. Cost</h2><p data-new="1">Sawaza is free to use: write records, send them and keep them, with no fees. If that ever changes, we will tell you in the app well before any charge applies, and nothing you already keep will be charged for.</p><h2>8. Acceptable use</h2><p data-new="1">Do not misuse Sawaza. That includes trying to reach records or accounts that are not yours, interfering with the service, copying or reselling it, sending unwanted records or invitations in bulk, or using it for anything unlawful, including fraud or money laundering. We may suspend or close an account that breaks these terms, and we will tell you why unless the law prevents us.</p><h2>9. The beta</h2><p data-new="1">Sawaza is in beta. We work to keep it running and your records safe, but the service may sometimes be unavailable, and features may change. We will tell you in the app before we remove anything you rely on.</p><h2>10. Our responsibility</h2><p data-new="1">We provide Sawaza as it is. To the extent the law allows, we are not responsible for losses that come from what users write in their records, from agreements between users, or from your phone being used by someone else. Nothing in these terms limits a right you have that the law does not allow us to limit.</p><h2>11. Ending</h2><p data-new="1">You can stop using Sawaza and delete your account from Settings at any time. Records confirmed with other people stay in their copy, as the <a href="/privacy">privacy policy</a> explains.</p><h2>12. The law and changes</h2><p data-new="1">These terms are governed by the laws of Uganda, and the courts of Uganda decide any dispute about them. If we change these terms, we will post the new version here with its date and tell you in the app before it takes effect. Questions go to hello@sawaza.app.</p>
  <div class="next-row"><a class="tlink" href="/privacy">Privacy policy <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>{PRELAUNCH ? <a class="tlink" href="/#contact">Contact <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a> : <a class="tlink" href="/help">Help <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>}</div>
</div></div></section>
</Base>
